Third-Party Software
--------------------

SAB is built on and bundles open-source software. The following libraries are
used in this project; each remains under its own license:

Python dependencies (runtime and build):
- Typer (MIT) — CLI framework
- LiteLLM (MIT) — multi-provider LLM support
- Rich (MIT) — terminal formatting
- pydantic (MIT) — data validation
- python-dotenv (BSD-3-Clause) — environment configuration
- FastAPI (MIT) — web framework
- uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause) — ASGI server
- websockets (BSD-3-Clause) — WebSocket support
- hatchling (MIT) — build backend

Web / front-end assets (bundled under /static/lib):
- highlight.js (BSD-3-Clause) — syntax highlighting
- KaTeX (MIT) — math rendering
- Mermaid (MIT) — diagram rendering
- Additional vendored libraries (xlsx, qrcode, mammoth, html2pdf, docx)
  remain under their respective licenses.

A complete dependency manifest with version pinning is maintained in
pyproject.toml. Please refer to each project's own license terms for the
precise obligations of that component.
